1. First handle block 0 (9 digits). If k <= 9, return k.
2. Otherwise, subtract 9, and find which block the digit falls into.
3. For blocks grouped by digit length d of b: blocks from 10^(d-1) to 10^d - 1, each contributing 10*(d+1) digits. There are 9*10^(d-1) such blocks.
